commit 2bbd25fcbb84270b775bdca60f532dabfeb4e9d2

C03: the scheduled alarms and reminders can be listed on request (AGENDA1435 infrastructure, BUILD1435)

«listá los timers» (H0262) was conditioned since AGENDA1337: only the due notifications could be listed (notification.list.due), never the scheduled ones.

Baxy.Kernel ProductCatalog: notification.list (limit 1..50), read-only, public, "windows.task.postread.v1", placed in ordinal order.
Baxy.Core ExternalCapabilityHandlers: routed to the external provider.
Baxy.Providers.Windows WindowsScheduledNotificationAdapter.ListAsync: runs the scheduler script in diagnose mode, keeps the BAXY-Alarm/BAXY-Reminder tasks whose next run lies in the future (a fired one-shot task keeps its registration without a next run and is counted as stale, not listed), reads each title from the ring script's base64, and reports kind, title, nextRunUtc and state, with count, staleTaskCount and the limit; WindowsExternalCapabilityProvider names the required adapter.
Baxy.App ObservedResponseLiterals: listed titles are observed data.
baxy_mind effect_intent: _notification_listing_request reads «listá los timers/alarmas», «qué alarmas tengo programadas», «what timers do I have» (never the due forms); __main__ grounds the empty argument object; llm projects count and scheduled items (kind label, title, next run in local time) and instructs to say that none are scheduled when the count is zero; observed_response_literals masks the titles; one alias example.

Offline probe: the literal and five variants resolve to notification.list; the due, schedule, cancel and prohibition forms do not; projection and the empty-count final pass the vetoes; the product compiles and the core advertises the operation. This PC currently holds 910 stale BAXY-Alarm tasks (fired, no next run): they are excluded from the count. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


